From 83e171a30b234a53f64c63a4faa89a52cc365e74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] docs(api): mark the API as beta instead of stable

The OpenAPI document, README, SECURITY.md and the v1.0 release notes
call 1.0.0 the first stable release with compatibility guaranteed
within the major version. That never held: in 1.0.x the runnable
entrypoint answered every business endpoint with 501 and nothing was
authenticated, and 1.1.0 already contains several breaking changes.

Mark the API as beta (info.x-stability) and set info.version to the
1.1.0 it describes. Add a section to the deprecation policy that states
what beta means: minor releases may break compatibility but must flag
it in the CHANGELOG, and the API goes back to stable only once the
acceptance criteria in architecture.md section 20 are met.
